// Title: Renamed AutoIt Execution
// ID: f4264e47-f522-4c38-a420-04525d5b880f
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-04
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed AutoIt2.exe or AutoIt3.exe.
// AutoIt is a scripting language and automation tool for Windows systems. While primarily used for legitimate automation tasks, it can be misused in cyber attacks.
// Attackers can leverage AutoIt to create and distribute malware, including keyloggers, spyware, and botnets. A renamed AutoIt executable is particularly suspicious.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((CommandLine = /* /AutoIt3ExecuteScript*/i or CommandLine = /* /ErrorStdOut*/i)) or ((Hashes = /*IMPHASH=FDC554B3A8683918D731685855683DDF*/i or Hashes = /*IMPHASH=CD30A61B60B3D60CECDB034C8C83C290*/i or Hashes = /*IMPHASH=F8A00C72F2D667D2EDBB234D0C0AE000*/i)) or ((OriginalFilename = "AutoIt3.exe" or OriginalFilename = "AutoIt2.exe" or OriginalFilename = "AutoIt.exe"))) and not(((ImageFileName = /.*\\AutoIt.exe/i or ImageFileName = /.*\\AutoIt2.exe/i or ImageFileName = /.*\\AutoIt3_x64.exe/i or ImageFileName = /.*\\AutoIt3.exe/i))))
